---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Sheet from '../../components/Sheet.astro';

const title = 'Essays: ModelDrift';
const description =
  'ModelDrift publishes one essay and video per major finding, starting with presence results from the August 2026 run. No essays are live yet. First one ships September 6, 2026.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <Sheet as="section">
    <span class="eyebrow">Essays</span>
    <h1>Essays</h1>
    <p>
      Five essays, each with an accompanying video, walk through what the <a href="/methodology"
        >runs</a
      > actually found. None are published yet; the first run hasn't happened. This page will list
      them here as they ship.
    </p>
  </Sheet>

  <Sheet as="section">
    <h2>First essay: September 6, 2026</h2>
    <p>
      The first essay covers <strong>presence</strong> from the August 12, 2026 run: across all
      five engines and five repetitions per question, which of the <a href="/companies"
        >tracked companies</a
      > actually get named for the 20 buyer questions, which never come up at all, and whether that
      breaks down differently for problem-aware questions versus head-to-head comparisons. The video
      walks through the same findings for anyone who'd rather watch than read.
    </p>
    <p>
      Accuracy and sourcing findings from the same run follow as separate essays later in
      September, once the coding pass on citations and claims is complete.
    </p>
  </Sheet>
</BaseLayout>
